data: {"type":"tool-output-available","toolCallId":"call-5c6970d9-32bc-4219-89b7-52ce5643f94c","output":{"output":"Found 36 matches in 4 files\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/recipes/format-dates.mdx:\n  7: ### formatDate\n  12: formatDate(date: Date, options?: {\n  28: By default, `formatDate` uses `{ mode: \"standard\", time: \"for today\", day: true, month: true, year: true, noToday: false }`. If the date is today, then `Today` is produced instead of the actual day in the locale language, and the time is appended because the default `time` option is `\"for today\"`. Pass `{ time: false }` to suppress the time for today's date, or `{ noToday: true }` to format today like any other date.\n  32: Here's an example of how to use `formatDate` with a `Date` object:\n  35: import { formatDate } from \"@openmrs/esm-framework\";\n  38:   return <span>{formatDate(appointment.scheduledDate, { mode: \"standard\" })}</span>;\n  46: Use `formatPartialDate` when a value may contain only a year or a year and month. This is common for approximate clinical dates. It parses the string using the current locale, hides date parts that were not present in the input, and then delegates formatting to `formatDate`.\n  63: `formatDatetime` accepts the same options as `formatDate` except for `time`, which is always included:\n  151: import { formatDate, parseDate } from \"@openmrs/esm-framework\";\n  154:   return <span>{formatDate(parseDate(encounter.encounterDateTime))}</span>;\n  190: O3 can format dates using locale-specific calendars. The app shell registers implementation-level calendar preferences from the styleguide `preferredCalendar` configuration, and `formatDate` also accepts a `calendar` option for one-off overrides.\n  58: ### formatDatetime\n  66: formatDatetime(date: Date, options?: Partial<Omit<FormatDateOptions, \"time\">>): string\n  69: Here's an example of how to use `formatDatetime`:\n  72: import { formatDatetime } from \"@openmrs/esm-framework\";\n  75:   return <span>{formatDatetime(appointment.scheduledDate)}</span>;\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/recipes/format-dates.mdx:\n  7: ### formatDate\n  12: formatDate(date: Date, options?: {\n  28: Par défaut, `formatDate` utilise `{ mode: \"standard\", time: \"for today\", day: true, month: true, year: true, noToday: false }`. Si la date est aujourd'hui, `Today` est produit à la place du jour réel dans la langue locale, et l'heure est ajoutée parce que l'option `time` vaut `\"for today\"` par défaut. Passez `{ time: false }` pour masquer l'heure pour la date du jour, ou `{ noToday: true }` pour formater aujourd'hui comme une date ordinaire.\n  32: Voici un exemple d'utilisation de `formatDate` avec un objet `Date` :\n  35: import { formatDate } from \"@openmrs/esm-framework\";\n  38:   return <span>{formatDate(appointment.scheduledDate, { mode: \"standard\" })}</span>;\n  46: Utilisez `formatPartialDate` lorsqu'une valeur peut ne contenir qu'une année, ou une année et un mois. C'est fréquent pour des dates cliniques approximatives. La fonction analyse la chaîne avec la locale courante, masque les parties absentes de l'entrée, puis délègue le formatage à `formatDate`.\n  63: `formatDatetime` accepte les mêmes options que `formatDate`, sauf `time`, qui est toujours inclus:\n  151: import { formatDate, parseDate } from \"@openmrs/esm-framework\";\n  154:   return <span>{formatDate(parseDate(encounter.encounterDateTime))}</span>;\n  190: O3 peut formater les dates avec des calendriers propres à une locale. Le shell de l'application enregistre les préférences de calendrier de l'implémentation depuis la configuration styleguide `preferredCalendar`, et `formatDate` accepte aussi une option `calendar` pour les remplacements ponctuels.\n  58: ### formatDatetime\n  66: formatDatetime(date: Date, options?: Partial<Omit<FormatDateOptions, \"time\">>): string\n  69: Voici un exemple d’utilisation de `formatDatetime` :\n  72: import { formatDatetime } from \"@openmrs/esm-framework\";\n  75:   return <span>{formatDatetime(appointment.scheduledDate)}</span>;\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/forms-in-o3/expressions-validation-and-logic.mdx:\n  44: | `formatDate(value, format?)` | A formatted string; throws when a non-`Date` value cannot be parsed. |\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/forms-in-o3/expressions-validation-and-logic.mdx:\n  41: | `formatDate(value, format?)` | Chaîne formatée; lève une erreur lorsqu'une valeur non-`Date` ne peut pas être analysée. |","sources":[{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/recipes/format-dates.mdx","name":"format-dates.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/recipes/format-dates.mdx","name":"format-dates.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/forms-in-o3/expressions-validation-and-logic.mdx","name":"expressions-validation-and-logic.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/forms-in-o3/expressions-validation-and-logic.mdx","name":"expressions-validation-and-logic.mdx","revision":"HEAD"}]}}

