data: {"type":"data-source","data":{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/recipes/format-dates.mdx","name":"format-dates.mdx","revision":"HEAD"}}

data: {"type":"tool-output-available","toolCallId":"call-cd98cb8d-c0c8-494c-a7d3-351f3cc53ac9","output":{"output":"<repo>github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs</repo>\n<path>content/en-US/docs/recipes/format-dates.mdx</path>\n<url>undefined</url>\n<content>\n121:   formatOptions: { style: \"long\" },\n122: }); // \"2 years, 6 months, 29 days\"\n123: ```\n124: \n125: The lower-level `duration` helper returns the structured `Intl.DurationInput` object instead of formatted text. It uses the same auto-selection thresholds as `formatDurationBetween` and accepts singular or plural unit names, such as `\"year\"` or `\"years\"`.\n126: \n127: ### isOmrsDateStrict\n128: \n129: This utility strictly checks whether a date string matches the OpenMRS payload date-time format. The format should be `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.SSSZZ`.\n130: It accepts an `omrsPayloadString` and returns a `boolean`.\n131: \n132: ```ts\n133:   isOmrsDateStrict(omrsPayloadString: string): boolean\n134: ```\n135: \n136: ### isOmrsDateToday\n137: \n138: This utility checks if the provided date is today. Accepts a `DateInput` and returns a `boolean`.\n139: \n140: ```ts\n141:   isOmrsDateToday(date: DateInput): boolean\n142: ```\n143: \n144: ### parseDate\n145: \n146: This utility function parses an arbitrary `dateString` into a `Date`. It uses `dayjs(dateString)`.\n147: \n148: Here's an example of how to use `parseDate` with an OpenMRS date-time string:\n149: \n150: ```tsx\n151: import { formatDate, parseDate } from \"@openmrs/esm-framework\";\n152: \n153: function EncounterDate({ encounter }: EncounterDateProps) {\n154:   return <span>{formatDate(parseDate(encounter.encounterDateTime))}</span>;\n155: }\n156: ```\n157: \n158: For an English locale, the returned value would be a string in the format `18-May-2023`.\n159: \n160: ### toDateObjectStrict\n161: \n162: This utility function converts an OpenMRS payload date-time string to a `Date` object. It accepts `omrsDateString` and returns a `Date` or `null`.\n163: \n164: ```ts\n165:   toDateObjectStrict(omrsDateString: string): Date | null\n166: ```\n167: \n168: ### toOmrsIsoString\n169: \n170: This utility function formats the input `date` to a `string` using the format `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.SSSZZ`. It is mostly used to format dates before submitting data in payloads.\n171: \n172: ```ts\n173:   toOmrsIsoString(date: DateInput, toUTC?: boolean): string\n174: ```\n175: \n176: The `toUTC` parameter is optional and defaults to `false`. When set to `true`, the date will be converted to UTC before formatting.\n177: \n178: Here's an example of how to use `toOmrsIsoString` in a payload:\n179: \n180: ```ts\n181: body: {\n182:   visit: visitUuid,\n183:   patientUuid: patientUuid,\n184:   startedAt: toOmrsIsoString(new Date()),\n185: }\n186: ```\n187: \n188: ### Locale calendars\n189: \n190: O3 can format dates using locale-specific calendars. The app shell registers implementation-level calendar preferences from the styleguide `preferredCalendar` configuration, and `formatDate` also accepts a `calendar` option for one-off overrides.\n191: \n192: Use `registerDefaultCalendar(locale, calendar)` to register a default calendar for a locale, `getDefaultCalendar(locale)` to inspect the resolved calendar, and `convertToLocaleCalendar(date, locale)` when working with `@internationalized/date` calendar values.\n193: \n\n(End of file - 193 lines total)\n</content>","sources":[{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/recipes/format-dates.mdx","name":"format-dates.mdx","revision":"HEAD"}]}}

data: {"type":"data-source","data":{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","path":"packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts","name":"date-util.ts","revision":"HEAD"}}

data: {"type":"tool-output-available","toolCallId":"call-446d2a9d-d01b-4315-ab07-31937790b78e","output":{"output":"<repo>github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core</repo>\n<path>packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts</path>\n<url>undefined</url>\n<content>\n100: \n101: /**\n102:  * Internal cache for per-locale calendars\n103:  */\n104: class LocaleCalendars {\n105:   #registry = new Map<string, CalendarIdentifier>();\n106: \n107:   constructor() {}\n108: \n109:   register(locale: string, calendar: CalendarIdentifier) {\n110:     this.#registry.set(locale, calendar);\n111:   }\n112: \n113:   getCalendar(locale: Intl.Locale): CalendarIdentifier | undefined {\n114:     if (!Boolean(locale)) {\n115:       return undefined;\n116:     }\n117: \n118:     if (locale.calendar) {\n119:       return locale.calendar as CalendarIdentifier;\n120:     }\n121: \n122:     if (locale.region) {\n123:       const key = `${locale.language}-${locale.region}`;\n124:       if (this.#registry.has(key)) {\n125:         return this.#registry.get(key);\n126:       }\n127:     }\n128: \n129:     if (locale.language && this.#registry.has(locale.language)) {\n\n(Showing lines 100-129 of 725. Use offset=130 to continue.)\n</content>","sources":[{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","path":"packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts","name":"date-util.ts","revision":"HEAD"}]}}

